{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"b66ae3df-24ff-4dc2-bd83-7593fd96a82c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have audited [server.py](file:///tmp/h-2YcopJ/server.py) against the Model Context Protocol (MCP) specification and real-world MCP client implementations (Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Gemini, Codex, and MCP SDK clients), without modifying the server.\n\nThe findings have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-2YcopJ/ANSWER.md). Key issues identified include:\n\n1. **HTTP 401 \u0026 Non-JSON-RPC Responses**:\n   - Unauthenticated calls to `add_note` and resources return raw HTTP `401` with non-JSON-RPC bodies (`{\"error\": \"sign in required\"}` / `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`), causing client JSON-RPC parsers to crash.\n2. **GET Endpoint Rejection (405 Method Not Allowed)**:\n   - Rejects HTTP `GET` requests with `405`, preventing clients from opening SSE streams as expected by the Streamable HTTP transport.\n3. **Protocol-level Error Codes (-32602) for Tool Execution Failures**:\n   - `get_note` throws a `-32602` JSON-RPC error when a note is not found instead of returning a standard tool result with `isError: true`, causing clients to treat normal business logic lookup misses as fatal protocol errors.\n4. **Unsupported Protocol Version String**:\n   - Returns `\"protocolVersion\": \"2025-06-18\"`, which fails version negotiation in clients expecting standard versions like `\"2024-11-05\"`.\n5. **Non-Standard Tool Result Schema**:\n   - Injects a top-level `\"structuredContent\"` field in `CallToolResult`, which causes validation failures in strict MCP client schema validators.\n","duration_seconds":198.160429,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":109310,"output_tokens":5159,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":358646,"total_tokens":114469}}}
